        "name": "USN-7852-2",
        "description": "USN-7582-1 fixed a vulnerability in libxml2. This update provides the corresponding fix for Ubuntu 16.04 LTS, Ubuntu 18.04 LTS and Ubuntu 20.04 LTS.  Original advisory details:   It was discovered that libxslt, used by libxml2, incorrectly handled  certain attributes. An attacker could use this issue to cause a crash,  resulting in a denial of service, or possibly execute arbitrary code. This  update adds a fix to libxml2 to mitigate the libxslt vulnerability.",
        "aliases": [
          "CVE-2025-7425"
        ]
      },
